  • ChargeTelemetryReading.{battery_temp,inside_temp,outside_temp} → MIGRATE to
    useUnits.formatTemperature display + lib.convertTempFromSI for chart values.
    These map from InsideTemp/OutsideTemp/ModuleTempMax (°C SI; UnitKindNone).
  • ChargingSession.miles_added → KEEP useSettings.convertDistance — same locked-policy
    pattern as Drive.distance_mi (Phase-43/0020): SQL adapter rounds the SI →
    miles boundary in charging_repo.go derive step. Out of phase-43 scope.
  • ChargeTelemetryReading.{rated_range,ideal_range,est_range} → KEEP useSettings.convertDistance —
    not populated by new backend (no chargeTelemetryFieldMappings entries); legacy
    rows from old data may still surface mi values. Defensive null-guard preserved.
  • ChargeTelemetryReading.{voltage,current_amps,power_kw,energy_added} → KEEP literal
    V/A/kW/kWh suffix display (vendor-passthrough; no settings-driven conversion exists).
  • ChargeTelemetryReading.charge_rate → not currently rendered by any features/charging
    page; leaving on its current (absent) display path. Still suffix-misleading.
  • ChargingTelemetry.{charge_rate_mph,charge_miles_added,battery_range_mi} →
    KEEP useSettings.convertDistance — Phase-43/0020 explicitly deferred this exact
    contract: "ChargingTelemetry.charge_* (ChargingTelemetrySection.tsx) are
    misleadingly-named — values are SI but field names suggest legacy units;
    reconciliation deferred to follow-up audit per PREFLIGHT NOTES." Same fields,
    same locked policy.
  • ChargingSession.cost / cost_currency / charger_power_kw_max/avg / energy_added_kwh →
    no unit-of-measure conversion needed (currency / kW / kWh are vendor-passthrough).

